From eede7870700fc1068e2b493178d5249aeeefc012 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Kelly <94ryan.kelly@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:13:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Iceberg-ready columns: field IDs, local timestamps,
 INT32 dates

- [ParquetColumn(FieldId = n)] writes DataField.FieldId (Parquet.Net 6 backend).
- [ParquetTimestamp(Microseconds, AdjustedToUtc = false)] writes TIMESTAMP(MICROS,
  isAdjustedToUTC=false) via DateTimeFormat.Timestamp; Parquet.Net ignores the flag
  for DateAndTimeMicros.
- DateOnly is written as INT32 DATE instead of INT96.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
